# Crew Environment Variables
# Copy to .crew/.env and fill in your values
# This file is sourced before each agent starts
#
# Naming convention:
#   {PROVIDER}_ANT_{FIELD} = Anthropic-compatible endpoint (for claude CLI)
#   {PROVIDER}_OAI_{FIELD} = OpenAI-compatible endpoint   (for codex CLI)
#   Fields: URL, MODEL, KEY

# ── Primary (Anthropic-compatible) ──
# 1ST_ANT_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
# 1ST_ANT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-20250514
# 1ST_ANT_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ── OpenAI / Codex ──
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# ── Gemini (Google) ──
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...

# ── 3rd Party: Anthropic-compatible ──
# Example: OpenRouter, DeepSeek, GLM, MiniMax, DashScope
# OPENROUTER_ANT_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# OPENROUTER_ANT_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-20250514
# OPENROUTER_ANT_KEY=sk-or-...

# ── 3rd Party: OpenAI-compatible (for codex CLI) ──
# Example: DashScope, MiniMax, local LLMs
# QW_OAI_URL=https://coding.dashscope.aliyuncs.com/v1
# QW_OAI_MODEL=qwen3.5-plus
# QW_OAI_KEY=sk-sp-...

# ── Model Configuration ──
# These can be overridden per-agent via crew.yaml `env` field.
# When using fallback, each level overrides these values.

# ── Fallback Order ──
# Configure in crew.yaml per-agent `fallback` array.
# Each level is tried in order when the previous level exhausts max_restarts.
# Fallback levels can also switch CLI types (e.g., claude -> codex).
#
# See crew.yaml for full configuration.
